# Caddy TLS edge for CYBER-SEC production (SEC-061).
# ACME automatic (HTTP-01) — zero-budget, no self-signed, no manual certs.
#
# STOCK IMAGE ONLY. This file loads on the official `caddy:2` image used by
# infra/prod/docker-compose.yml. Caddy's `rate_limit` directive is NOT part of
# the standard build (it requires a custom xcaddy image and a stock `caddy:2`
# container rejects the file with "unknown directive: rate_limit"), so login
# brute-force limiting is enforced in the app instead — app/ratelimit.py,
# SEC-073 — where it is testable and works in every deployment. An optional
# second, edge-level layer is documented in infra/README.md.
$DOMAIN {
	encode gzip zstd

	# /metrics is platform posture data (open alert counts by severity, DB
	# size, session counts). The app binds to the internal address only, so
	# scrape it from the host or the internal network:
	#   curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/metrics
	# It is never served on the public edge.
	@metrics path /metrics
	respond @metrics 403

	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		Referrer-Policy "no-referrer"
		-Server
	}

	reverse_proxy cybersec:8080 {
		# Preserve the real client for the app's per-IP login limiter and
		# session attribution (ForwardedHeadersMiddleware trusts one hop).
		header_up X-Real-IP {http.request.remote.host}
	}
}
